# Scalability and observability

## Backend (Firestore / API)

- Use **cursor pagination** (default limit 20, max 100). Honor `STRICT_QUERY_PAGINATION` where enabled.
- After new list/query shapes: `pnpm generate:firestore-indexes` and keep `pnpm check:firestore-indexes` green. See `docs/guides/dynamic-firestore-indexes.md`.
- No unbounded collection scans in handlers/workers. Prefer indexed queries.
- Eliminate N+1: batch with `getAll` / multi-get / redesign joins. See `docs/guides/relational-data-system.md`.
- In-process TTL caches via `@repo/shared-types` `createTtlCache` (roles, user access, entity definitions). Invalidate on writes. Env: `CACHE_TTL_MS`.
- Rate limit via `@fastify/rate-limit` (`API_RATE_LIMIT_*`). Compress JSON responses.
- Aggregations and metrics: follow `docs/guides/aggregations.md` and `docs/guides/metrics-consumption.md` — do not recompute expensive rollups on every request.

## Frontend

- TanStack Query: sensible `staleTime`, invalidate on mutations; catalog refresh patterns in `apps/web` / `docs/guides/performance-scaling.md`.
- Virtualize long lists (`@tanstack/react-virtual`); debounce filter inputs (~300ms).
- Rely on RR7 route-module code splitting; avoid shipping huge eager charts/entity trees.

## Observability

- Structured request timing (`ENABLE_PERF_LOGS`: `rbacMs`, `queryMs`, `hooksMs`, `totalMs`).
- Prefer structured logs suitable for Cloud Logging; avoid noisy debug in hot loops.
- AI jobs: inspect `/debugger/ai-jobs`; use workload run lineage for async work.

## Do not

- Add Redis / new distributed infra without an explicit platform decision (Phase B items stay deferred unless planned)
- Ship admin APIs that return entire tenants without pagination
- Ignore missing-index hints in logs

## Enforcement

- `docs/guides/performance-scaling.md`
- `pnpm check:firestore-indexes`, API/web tests
- `pnpm --filter api test`, `pnpm --filter web test`

